{"name":"Red Onion","hex":"#473442","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"red onion","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of onion with reddish purplish skin.","An instance of this type."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red_onion"}],"entries":[{"title":"Red Onion, Kansas","blocks":[{"text":"Red Onion is an unincorporated community in Crawford County, Kansas, United States."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_Onion%2C_Kansas","wikidata":"Q18393771"},{"title":"The Red Onion","blocks":[{"text":"The Red Onion is a restaurant located on East Cooper Avenue in Aspen, Colorado, United States. It is the oldest restaurant in the city, housed in a three-story red brick Italianate building dating to the late 19th century. In 1987 it was listed on the National Register of Historic Places as \"New Brick–The Brick Saloon\", along with other historic properties in the city. It is currently closed; there are several efforts underway to reopen it."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/66/Red_Onion_Logo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Red_Onion","wikidata":"Q7759907"},{"title":"Red onion","blocks":[{"text":"Red onions are cultivars of the onion, and have purplish-red skin and white flesh tinged with red. They are most commonly used in cooking, but the skin has also been used as a dye."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Red_onions_11.jpg/330px-Red_onions_11.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_onion","wikidata":"Q622350"},{"title":"Onion","blocks":[{"text":"The onion, also known as the bulb onion or common onion, is a vegetable that is the most widely cultivated species of the genus Allium. The shallot is a botanical variety of the onion which was classified as a separate species until 2011. The onion's close 